{"ref":"BDB, סוּךְ","hw":"סוּךְ","html":"† I. <big><big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">סוּךְ</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">סִיךְ</span>]</big></big>  <strong>vb. pour</strong> in anointing, <strong>anoint (</strong>NH Aramaic <span dir=\"rtl\">סוּךְ</span> <em>anoint</em><strong>)</strong>;—<br><strong>Qal</strong>  Pf. 2 fs. <span dir=\"rtl\">וָסַכְתְּ</span> consec. <a data-ref=\"Ruth 3:3\" href=\"/Ruth.3.3\">Ru 3:3</a>; 1 s. <span dir=\"rtl\">סָ֑כְתִּי</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 10:3\" href=\"/Daniel.10.3\">Dn 10:3</a>; Impf. 2 ms. <span dir=\"rtl\">תָּסוּךְ</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 28:40\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.28.40\">Dt 28:40</a> <a data-ref=\"Micah 6:15\" href=\"/Micah.6.15\">Mi 6:15</a>; 2 fs. <span dir=\"rtl\">תָּסוּכִי</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 14:2\" href=\"/II_Samuel.14.2\">2 S 14:2</a>; 1 s. sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">וָאֲסֻכֵֿךְ</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:9\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.9\">Ez 16:9</a>; 3 mpl. sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">וַיְסֻכוּם</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 28:15\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.28.15\">2 Ch 28:15</a>; also (prob.) 3 ms. <span dir=\"rtl\">וַיָּ֫סֶךְ</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 12:20\" href=\"/II_Samuel.12.20\">2 S 12:20</a> (Ges<sup>§ 73 f.</sup>); Inf. abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">סוֹךְ</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 10:3\" href=\"/Daniel.10.3\">Dn 10:3</a>; appar. Impf. pass. is <span dir=\"rtl\">יִיסָ֔ךְ</span> read <span dir=\"rtl\">יוסך</span> Sam. (Kö<sup>i.436</sup>) <a data-ref=\"Exodus 30:32\" href=\"/Exodus.30.32\">Ex 30:32</a> (and not <strong>Hoph.</strong>, cf. Ges<sup>l.c.</sup>);—<em>anoint</em>, in the toilet, often after washing; usually <strong>1.</strong>  refl. <em>anoint oneself</em>, <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 12:20\" href=\"/II_Samuel.12.20\">2 S 12:20</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ruth 3:3\" href=\"/Ruth.3.3\">Ru 3:3</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">סוֹךְ לֹא־סָ֑כְתִּי</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 10:3\" href=\"/Daniel.10.3\">Dn 10:3</a>; + <span dir=\"rtl\">שֶׁמֶן</span> as acc. mat. <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 14:2\" href=\"/II_Samuel.14.2\">2 S 14:2</a> <a data-ref=\"Micah 6:15\" href=\"/Micah.6.15\">Mi 6:15</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 28:40\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.28.40\">Dt 28:40</a>. <strong>2.</strong>  act., <em>anoint</em> another <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:9\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.9\">Ez 16:9</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">(בַּשֶּׁמֶן)</span>, <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 28:15\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.28.15\">2 Ch 28:15</a>. <strong>3.</strong>  pass., <em>be poured</em>, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 30:32\" href=\"/Exodus.30.32\">Ex 30:32</a> (P; subj. the sacred oil).","next":"BDB, אָסוּךְ²","prev":"BDB, סוֹטַי"}